Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the codebase. Let me provide a detailed implementation plan for organization management with member invitations.

---

# Implementation Plan: Organization Management with Member Invitations

## Overview

This plan outlines the implementation of a complete organization management system including member listing, invitations, role management, and invitation acceptance. The implementation leverages the existing Better Auth organizations plugin and follows the established patterns in the codebase.

## 1. File Structure

```
apps/web/src/
├── app/(app)/
│   ├── settings/
│   │   ├── organization/
│   │   │   └── page.tsx                    # Organization settings page
│   │   └── layout.tsx                      # Settings layout (optional)
│   └── invitations/
│       └── [invitationId]/
│           └── page.tsx                    # Invitation accept/reject page
│
├── components/
│   └── organization/
│       ├── index.ts                        # Barrel export
│       ├── types.ts                        # Shared types
│       ├── member-list/
│       │   ├── index.ts                    # Barrel export
│       │   ├── member-list.tsx             # Main member list component
│       │   ├── member-row.tsx              # Individual member row
│       │   ├── member-actions-menu.tsx     # Actions dropdown for members
│       │   └── member-skeleton.tsx         # Loading skeleton
│       ├── invitation-list/
│       │   ├── index.ts                    # Barrel export
│       │   ├── invitation-list.tsx         # Pending invitations list
│       │   └── invitation-row.tsx          # Individual invitation row
│       ├── invite-member-dialog/
│       │   ├── index.ts                    # Barrel export
│       │   ├── invite-member-dialog.tsx    # Desktop dialog
│       │   ├── invite-member-sheet.tsx     # Mobile sheet variant
│       │   └── invite-member-form.tsx      # Shared form logic
│       ├── role-badge.tsx                  # Badge component for roles
│       └── hooks/
│           ├── use-organization-members.ts # Query hook for members
│           ├── use-invitations.ts          # Query hook for invitations
│           └── use-member-actions.ts       # Mutation hooks for actions
```

## 2. Page Routes

### 2.1 Organization Settings Page
**Route:** `/settings/organization`
**File:** `apps/web/src/app/(app)/settings/organization/page.tsx`

This page will contain:
- Organization info section (name, logo, slug)
- Tabs or sections for:
  - Members tab (default)
  - Invitations tab
  - General settings tab (future)

### 2.2 Invitation Acceptance Page
**Route:** `/invitations/[invitationId]`
**File:** `apps/web/src/app/(app)/invitations/[invitationId]/page.tsx`

This page will:
- Show invitation details (organization name, inviter, role)
- Display accept/reject buttons
- Handle authenticated and unauthenticated users differently
- Show error state for expired/invalid invitations

## 3. Component Composition Approach

### 3.1 Compound Component Pattern

The organization components will follow a compound component pattern similar to the existing `Card` and `Dialog` components:

```typescript
// Example: MemberList compound component
<MemberList>
  <MemberListHeader>
    <MemberListTitle>Team Members</MemberListTitle>
    <MemberListActions>
      <InviteMemberDialog />
    </MemberListActions>
  </MemberListHeader>
  <MemberListContent>
    <MemberListTable />
  </MemberListContent>
</MemberList>
```

### 3.2 Responsive Design Pattern

Use `useIsMobile` hook to conditionally render Dialog vs Sheet:

```typescript
// Based on existing patterns in app-header.tsx
function InviteMemberModal() {
  const isMobile = useIsMobile();
  const [open, setOpen] = useState(false);

  if (isMobile) {
    return (
      <Sheet open={open} onOpenChange={setOpen}>
        <SheetTrigger>...</SheetTrigger>
        <SheetContent>
          <InviteMemberForm onSuccess={() => setOpen(false)} />
        </SheetContent>
      </Sheet>
    );
  }

  return (
    <Dialog open={open} onOpenChange={setOpen}>
      <DialogTrigger>...</DialogTrigger>
      <DialogContent>
        <InviteMemberForm onSuccess={() => setOpen(false)} />
      </DialogContent>
    </Dialog>
  );
}
```

### 3.3 Form Pattern

Follow existing `@tanstack/react-form` + Zod pattern from `create-organization-form.tsx`:

```typescript
const form = useForm({
  defaultValues: { email: "", role: "member" },
  onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {
    // Call authClient.organization.inviteMember
  },
  validators: {
    onSubmit: z.object({
      email: z.string().email("Invalid email address"),
      role: z.enum(["member", "admin"]),
    }),
  },
});
```

## 4. Key Implementation Details

### 4.1 Member List Component

**File:** `apps/web/src/components/organization/member-list/member-list.tsx`

```typescript
// Key features:
// - Fetch members using authClient.organization.listMembers()
// - Display avatar, name, email, role, joined date
// - Show loading skeletons during fetch
// - Responsive: Table on desktop, Card list on mobile
// - Sort by role (owner > admin > member), then by name
```

**Data fetching approach:**
```typescript
// Use React Query via TanStack Query (already used in project)
const { data: members, isLoading, refetch } = useQuery({
  queryKey: ["organization-members", organizationId],
  queryFn: async () => {
    const result = await authClient.organization.listMembers({
      organizationId,
    });
    if (result.error) throw new Error(result.error.message);
    return result.data;
  },
  enabled: !!organizationId,
});
